<title>PERU: Peru lifts 9-month ban on used vehicle imports.</title>
<headline>Peru lifts 9-month ban on used vehicle imports.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Peruvian government lifted with immediate effect from Friday a nine-month ban on the importation of used vehicles.</p>
<p>Under new regulations, imported used cars cannot be more than five years' old, while imported buses and trucks have an eight-year limit.</p>
<p>The ban was originally intended to help ease Peru's large commercial deficit and the flooding of the local automobile market with imported used cars.</p>
<p>In an effort to stimulate development of its regional ports, the government has offered strong tax incentives for the importation of vehicles at Ilo and Matarani in the south, and Paita in the north.</p>
<p>-- Renzo Pipoli, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
